# T07 — Phase 1 — Identity resolver with ambiguity diagnostics

**Phase:** 1
**Type:** backend
**Model class:** balanced
**Depends on:** T06
**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 1: Unified Identity Model](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-1-unified-identity-model)
**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).

## Goal

This task implements the resolver that turns user-supplied or LLM-supplied references — paths, qualified symbol names, doc headings, test names, event refs — into the stable `Identity` values defined in T06. Spec §Phase 1 names "identity resolver for paths, symbols, headings, tests, and event refs" as a deliverable and binds the resolver to return ambiguity diagnostics rather than arbitrary matches when an input has multiple candidate identities. Without this resolver, every later phase would re-implement name→id lookups inconsistently, and ambiguity would be silently swallowed.

## Spec excerpts that drive this task

> "Phase 1 Deliverables: ... identity resolver for paths, symbols, headings, tests, and event refs ... compatibility support for legacy name-based references."

> "Definition of done: every workflow output can be expanded through a stable identity; ambiguous names return ambiguity diagnostics instead of arbitrary matches."

## Inputs

- Dependency outputs: identity types from T06 (`daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/kinds.rs`, `encoding.rs`).
- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:
  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/graph/` (workspace graph that backs path/symbol lookups)
  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/storage/` (SQLite-backed lookups for files, symbols, docs, sections)
  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/parser/` (doc heading and symbol extraction the resolver consumes)
- Standards files to honor: `coding.md` hard limits, naming (intent over mechanism), error handling (resolver errors must be structured, never silent); `AGENTS.md` (resolver public API is binding once shipped — any change is a contract change).

## Steps

1. Create `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/resolver.rs` with a `pub struct IdentityResolver` that holds references to the graph, storage, and parser indexes needed to answer lookups.
2. Define the resolver public API:
   - `resolve_path(&self, workspace: &WorkspaceId, path: &str) -> Result<FileId, ResolveError>`
   - `resolve_symbol(&self, workspace: &WorkspaceId, qualified_name: &str) -> ResolveOutcome<SymbolId>`
   - `resolve_section(&self, workspace: &WorkspaceId, doc: &DocId, heading: &str) -> ResolveOutcome<SectionId>`
   - `resolve_test(&self, workspace: &WorkspaceId, test_name: &str) -> ResolveOutcome<SymbolId>` (tests are identified as symbols with a `Test` kind)
   - `resolve_event_ref(&self, workspace: &WorkspaceId, ref_str: &str) -> Result<EventId, ResolveError>`
3. Create `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/ambiguity.rs` with the `ResolveOutcome<T>` enum (`Unique(T)`, `Ambiguous(AmbiguityReport<T>)`, `NotFound(ResolveError)`) and the `AmbiguityReport<T>` struct carrying the list of candidates plus a `disambiguation_hint` describing how the caller can narrow the query (suggest adding parent module, file path, byte offset, etc.).
4. The resolver must never pick arbitrarily when multiple matches exist — return `Ambiguous`. Tests in T09 will assert this on duplicate symbol names.
5. Add a legacy compatibility helper `pub fn resolve_legacy_symbol_name(&self, name: &str) -> ResolveOutcome<SymbolId>` that takes a name without workspace context and routes to the resolver via the default workspace, preserving older MCP payloads.
6. Implement caching: keep a small LRU keyed by `(workspace, query)` so the same resolution within a session does not re-traverse the graph. Cache hits must still preserve ambiguity semantics — a cached `Ambiguous` returns `Ambiguous`.
7. Errors are structured: `ResolveError::WorkspaceNotIndexed`, `ResolveError::Malformed`, `ResolveError::IndexLagBehind { latest_event_id }`. No bare `String` errors.
8. Add module-level docs in both files citing spec §Phase 1.
9. Register the new submodules in `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/mod.rs` with `pub mod resolver;` and `pub mod ambiguity;`.
10. Write smoke unit tests inline (the full ambiguity / rename / branch-change test matrix is owned by T09): construct a tiny resolver fixture and assert `resolve_path` returns a `FileId`, `resolve_symbol` on a duplicate name returns `Ambiguous`, and `resolve_legacy_symbol_name` falls back correctly.

## Files expected

- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/resolver.rs` — `IdentityResolver` struct, the five `resolve_*` methods, LRU cache, structured `ResolveError`.
- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/ambiguity.rs` — `ResolveOutcome<T>`, `AmbiguityReport<T>`, `disambiguation_hint` helpers.

## Verification

- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/resolver.rs` — confirms the resolver file exists.
- `cd daemon && cargo build -p lattice-core` — confirms the crate compiles with the resolver and ambiguity modules wired into `lattice-core`.
- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib identity::resolver` — confirms the resolver smoke tests pass.
- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib identity::ambiguity` — confirms the ambiguity module tests pass.

## Coding-standard checks

- File length ≤800 lines (verify with `wc -l daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/resolver.rs daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/ambiguity.rs`).
- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10 — every `resolve_*` method must fit; extract candidate-collection helpers if needed.
- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code.
- No unjustified `// allow(...)` or suppressions.
- Public API names follow intent-over-mechanism naming (`resolve_symbol` not `lookup`, `AmbiguityReport` not `MultiResult`).
- For schema changes: not applicable (resolver consumes existing storage).
- Doc citation: cite the exact `## Phase 1: Unified Identity Model` heading from the spec in module docs; if any non-obvious caching or LRU choice is made, cite the heading from `docs/architecture/2026-04-11-stable-follow-up-handles.md` that authorizes the behavior (per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` § Markdown Heading References).

## Definition of done

- [ ] Every file in "Files expected" exists with real content (no stubs).
- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.
- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.
- [ ] No deferred work: no item from spec §Phase 1 punted to a later phase.
- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md "Backward-compatibility and contract discipline" section was followed and the architecture doc was updated in the same task.

